title: Start
---
This is an example of using Yarn Spinner for a string of dialouge.
The dialouge can continue.
More dialouge can be written.
Narrator: This is an example of labeling who is speaking.
Other Narrator: This is an example of changing who is speaking.
This is an example of options.
<<declare $selectedOption1 = false>>
    -> This is an option.
        <<set $selectedOption1 to true>>
        You selected the first option.
        Why did you select this option? I told you to pick the second option.
        -> My bad.
            It's okay. Now I was able to show you what nesting options look like.
            Next is the jump, I will show you what a jump in dialouge looks like.
            <<jump Jump>>
        -> I knew what I was doing.
            Oh really. Maybe you did. I was able to show you what nesting options look like.
            Next is the jump, I will show you what a jump in dialouge looks like.
            <<jump Jump>>
    -> This is another option. Click this one to select it.
        You selected the second option.
        Next is the jump, I will show you what a jump in dialouge looks like.
        <<jump Jump>>

===

title: Jump
---
The dialouge just jumped!
Earlier when selecting an option, you picked option one. This statment is {$selectedOption1}.
===